# Rules in this file exist only to replace native ORCA logical xforms. Each
# rule must be independently proved before admission and carry causal E2E.
# Line 1 replaces the grouping-subset branch of CXformCollapseGbAgg, including
# equal grouping sets. Proj* admits only pure, unsplit global dedup aggregates.
# WeTune ProveDslRule: EQ, SQLSOLVER, verified 2026-08-28.
# Lines 11 and 13 cover the complete output space of CXformCollapseProject:
# the first moves every independent upper Compute definition into the lower
# layer; the second moves the maximal safe subset and retains a real residual.
# Both exact RuleIR strings are outcome-equivalence proof inputs accepted by
# the FormalSQL/Rocq 9.2 kernel on 2026-08-28. ExprConcat/ExprSplit remain
# explicit semantic premises checked generically against the live project
# lists; neither rule is identified by C++ code.
# Lines 15, 17, 19, 21, and 23 remove a pure DISTINCT from the inner relation
# of positive IN, EXISTS, NOT EXISTS, ANY, and ALL respectively. The ordinary
# target Proj preserves the complete
# SELECT-list/schema proof binding; pgORCA lowers that pass-through view to the
# native bare relational child. All three exact rules returned EQ from WeTune's
# SQLSolver backend; NOT EXISTS was verified on 2026-08-29 through its generic
# RuleIR/U-expression operator rather than a rule-specific proof path.
# ANY/ALL bind the complete comparison predicate; their exact rules were also
# proved EQ by the generic SQLSolver U-expression backend on 2026-08-29.
# Line 9 covers the equality branch of
# CXformLeftSemiJoin2InnerJoin. InSubFilter is the shared view over both the
# pre-unnest form and CLogicalLeftSemiJoin; the target deduplicates the inner
# key before joining, preserving semi-join bag multiplicity.
# WeTune ProveDslRule: EQ, SQLSOLVER, verified 2026-08-28.
# Line 5 is the proved InnerJoin branch of CXformPushJoinBelowLeftUnionAll.
# Complete source Join output binding lets the new target Union preserve the
# parent row, while shared positional mapping remaps predicates and freshens
# repeated target inputs. WeTune ProveDslRule: EQ, SQLSOLVER, 2026-08-28.
# Line 7 is the independently proved LeftJoin branch of the same xform.
# It distributes only across the preserved (left) input; right-side LeftJoin
# distribution is intentionally excluded because it is not bag-equivalent.
# WeTune ProveDslRule: EQ, SQLSOLVER, verified 2026-08-28.
# Line 3 replaces CXformUnion2UnionAll. The explicit Union output binding makes
# Proj* a full-row identity dedup rather than an arbitrary subset projection.
# WeTune ProveDslRule: EQ, SQLSOLVER, verified 2026-08-28.
